{
  "_doc": [
    "Per-class follower attractor tables. At 9th level, a PC's stronghold",
    "begins attracting class-specific followers per acore_axioms_strongholds_and_domains.xml",
    "§followers_arrival L111-116 (half rounded up at half-built; quarter rounded up",
    "at completion; remainder during the first month after completion).",
    "Counts are extracted verbatim from the class XML §stronghold_and_followers blocks.",
    "Each entry's `unit_template_id` references data/troops/unit_templates.json — the",
    "follower wave is materialized as one or more troop_units rows of that template.",
    "0th-level / apprentice / leader entries are followers of the named-class type per",
    "pc_followers_tables_rules.xml §general_rules; v1 lumps them into the soldier-",
    "tier mercenary equivalents until the equipment-table roll subsystem lands.",
    "race='matches_ruler' means the follower race matches the ruling character's race",
    "per acore_axioms §peasants_and_followers L107 (\"Families are of the same race",
    "as the adventurer\")."
  ],
